{"id":"chatcmpl-caa92736-1892-4de4-bf3d-85a8c785d336","object":"chat.completion","created":1795230022,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When forced-choice medical imaging questions conflict with unanimous negative tool outputs, the successful strategy was to escalate through multiple specialized models, then fall back to direct pixel inspection via a verifier rather than trusting tool consensus. The key insight is that automated detectors often miss subtle findings, so forced-choice framing should trigger deeper verification rather than acceptance of 'no finding' results.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Escalation pattern: when initial grounding/detection tools return negative results but the question forces a choice, progressively query additional specialized models before concluding.\",\n    \"Laterality disambiguation pattern: use image markers and anatomical landmarks (e.g., gastric bubble, 'L' marker) to map image-left/right to patient-left/right when assessing side-specific findings.\",\n    \"Conflict resolution pattern: when tool outputs contradict the forced-choice structure, invoke a verifier to re-examine raw pixels directly rather than defaulting to tool consensus.\",\n    \"Subtle-finding skepticism pattern: treat unanimous 'no finding' outputs as potentially false negatives when the task guarantees a positive answer exists among options.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging VQA\": \"Chain multiple specialized models (grounding, expert VQA, general medical VQA) and use a verifier for direct pixel inspection when tools disagree with forced-choice framing.\",\n    \"Forced-choice diagnostic tasks\": \"Assume one option is correct; if tools report absence, suspect subtle findings and re-inspect regions of interest at higher zoom before answering.\",\n    \"Laterality-sensitive detection\": \"Always anchor left/right to patient anatomy using markers and landmarks, not image coordinates, and cross-check with zoomed crops.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Before accepting a negative tool result, confirm the task guarantees a positive answer and re-inspect the relevant region at higher zoom.\",\n    \"Before finalizing laterality, verify patient-side mapping using radiological markers and anatomical landmarks (gastric bubble, liver shadow).\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":708,"total_tokens":1121,"completion_tokens":413,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":708},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":413}}}